Description: Report startup errors of the endpoints in tracker-serialize-test instead of waiting forever.
 The test starts a D-Bus and an HTTP endpoint, the latter on the fixed port 54322, in a thread, and the main thread
 polled a flag which the thread set only when both started. When one of them failed to start, the thread returned
 without setting it, and the test waited until meson killed it after 210 seconds, which failed a build of the package
 in the test serialize without saying why. The thread now reports its result through a queue, and the test fails at
 once with the error, like "Error binding to address 0.0.0.0:54322: Address already in use" when the port is taken.
 This is upstream's commit, with the declaration of retval added to main(), which upstream declares since a later
 commit. It changes only the test.
Author: ooonea <ooonea@gmail.com>
Origin: backport, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/tinysparql/-/commit/064f437913299c55ca5cc503bc029848be9379cb
